From: Mahdi Taziki <61482609+Mhd-tz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Reassert the hidden cursor on movement in an active fullscreen window.

When a fullscreen game hides the cursor and the pointer reaches the bottom screen edge, native macOS UI (the Dock or
menu bar reveal) can show the system arrow again while winemac's cursorHidden cache still says hidden, so the arrow
stays on top of the game's own cursor after moving back in (Unity 6 game, Mothville). On mouse movement in an active
fullscreen window whose client wants the cursor hidden, balance the earlier hide and let updateCursor hide it again,
so NSCursor's hide count doesn't grow. Supported NSCursor calls only.

Provenance (recorded by AnvilMac, 2026-10-16):
  Written for AnvilMac (investigation by OpenAI Codex, reviewed by Claude Code); not submitted upstream.
  Base: wine-11.19, commit 455e3509b98a. File: dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m (Wine, LGPL-2.1-or-later).
  License of this change: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Copyright 2026 Mahdi Taziki.
  Checked: the project owner reproduced the extra arrow at the bottom edge without it and confirmed it gone with it,
  with the normal pointer back outside the game. Wider checks (flicker, performance, multiple displays) pending.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -1471,4 +1471,13 @@
         else
             lastTargetWindow = nil;
 
+        /* Native screen-edge UI can reveal the cursor while our cache remains
+           hidden. Reassert the hide without accumulating NSCursor hide calls. */
+        if (lastTargetWindow.fullscreen && [NSApp isActive] &&
+            clientWantsCursorHidden && cursorHidden)
+        {
+            [NSCursor unhide];
+            cursorHidden = FALSE;
+        }
+
         [self updateCursor:FALSE];
